## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Limits and continuity)
## DBsection(Continuity - concept of)
## KEYWORDS('continuity','interval')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(2)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('1.5')
## Problem1('30')

#Problem APEX 1.5.30

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", 'PGML.pl', "PGcourse.pl");

Context("Interval");

$a      = random(1, 10) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$b      = random(1, 10) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$domain = Interval("(-inf,inf)");

BEGIN_PGML
Let [`` f(\theta) = [$a] \cos(\theta) + [$b] \sin(\theta) ``].

Give the interval(s) on which [`f(\theta)`] is continuous. [__]{$domain}

[@ helpLink("interval","Help with interval notation") @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Both [` \cos(\theta) `] and [` \sin(\theta)`] are continuous for all real numbers, so [`f`] will be also.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

